<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tangier</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tingis, Tanger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tangier is a port city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-gibraltar">Strait of Gibraltar</a>. As Tingis it was a Phoenician and Mauretanian town and the capital of the Roman province of Mauretania Tingitana. Later ruled by Muslim dynasties, Portugal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Morocco, it was an international zone from 1923 to 1956 and remains Morocco's main gateway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tangier.jpg" alt="Tangier" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ifni95 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanger_cor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A powerful navy, based at Almería, Seville and other ports, patrolled the coasts against Fatimid and Viking attacks and supported the North African campaigns, including the occupation of <b>Tangier</b> in 951.</blockquote><a href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Battle of Fakhkh, near Mecca, between the Abbasids and the supporters of Muhammad's descendants, he fled west, reached <b>Tangier</b> and by 788 had settled at Volubilis, Walili in Arabic.</blockquote><a href="/empire/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1912 the Treaty of Fez made it a French protectorate, with Spanish zones in the north and the Sahara and <b>Tangier</b> an international zone; the sultan kept formal sovereignty under colonial control, and tens of thousands of settlers took the richest farmland.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-morocco">Kingdom of Morocco · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>He recovered <b>Tangier</b>, La Mamora and Larache from Europeans.</blockquote><a href="/state/alaouite-sultanate">Alaouite Sultanate</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1661 the Kingdom of Portugal ceded <b>Tangier</b> to Charles II of the Kingdom of England as part of the dowry of Catherine of Braganza.</blockquote><a href="/state/english-tangier">English Tangier</a></li><li><blockquote>The kingdom lay west of the Mulucha (Moulouya) river and included old Phoenician towns such as Lixus and <b>Tingis</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-mauretania">Kingdom of Mauretania</a></li></ul></section>
